\newlabel{fig:splash}{{1}{2}{Two-colour Zig-Zag Numberlink on a $7 \times 10$ rectangle. Left, an instance with endpoints $s_0, t_0$ of colour~$0$ (green) and $s_1, t_1$ of colour~$1$ (orange). Middle, a solution. The two vertex-disjoint paths $s_0 \to t_0$ and $s_1 \to t_1$ together visit every cell, and the colour-$0$ path winds around the colour-$1$ path. Right, an unsolvable instance. The endpoints alternate in colour around the border, so the two paths would have to cross (catalogue entry \ent {T1}, Section~\ref {sec:catalogue}).\relax }{figure.caption.2}{}}
